Chapter: ScheduleParseGuard
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Schedule

 Track D item 19, the Schedule leg. This chapter's parser has NO memory-safety
 defect: eighteen malformed inputs were run against it before this arm was
 written and every one of them either answered None or returned a Sched, with
 no fault of any kind. Its index checks are complete.

 What it did instead was ACCEPT. Four shapes of malformed text produced a
 well-formed schedule that was not the one written:

 An unrecognised day name became Sunday, because sched-parse-day-name's final
 else answered 0. "weekly on wendsday at 9am" is a misspelling, and it
 scheduled.

 A between clause too short to parse was DROPPED rather than refused, because
 the n >= 6 test guarded the whole clause instead of the clause's arguments.
 "every 5 minutes between 9am" asked for a window and got an unrestricted
 schedule that runs all day.

 A between clause ending at "and" defaulted its stop hour to 24, and
 sched-format-hour renders 24 as "12pm". "every 5 minutes between 9am and"
 printed "between 9am and 12pm" and ran until midnight.

 Hours and minutes were unbounded, so "daily at 99999:99999" parsed.

 Rows 1 to 4 are the controls and they carry the whole weight of the range
 checks: every legitimate form this chapter documents must still parse, or a
 guard that answered None to everything would pass every hostile row.

Section: Helpers

  row : Text, Text -> Text
  row (label) (s) =
    when schedule s
      is None -> label & " None"
      is Just (sc) -> label & " " & format-sched sc

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (row "01-daily" "daily at 9:30am")
    print-line-uni (row "02-daily-pm" "daily at 2:30 pm")
    print-line-uni (row "03-weekly" "weekly on monday at 9am")
    print-line-uni (row "04-between" "every 5 minutes between 9am and 5pm")
    print-line-uni (row "05-midnight" "daily at 12:00am")
    print-line-uni (row "06-monthly-31" "monthly on 31 at 11:59pm")
    print-line-uni (row "07-bad-day" "weekly on notaday at 9am")
    print-line-uni (row "08-misspelled" "weekly on wendsday at 9am")
    print-line-uni (row "09-between-short" "every 5 minutes between 9am")
    print-line-uni (row "10-between-and" "every 5 minutes between 9am and")
    print-line-uni (row "11-huge-time" "daily at 99999:99999")
    print-line-uni (row "12-minute-99" "daily at 9:99am")
    print-line-uni (row "13-monthly-99" "monthly on 99 at 9am")
    print-line-uni (row "14-monthly-0" "monthly on 0 at 9am")
    print-line-uni (row "15-every-plain" "every 5 minutes")
  end

